# The wrapper script must stay LF whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf is set to: CRLF line
# endings make it unrunnable on the Linux CI runner.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary

# Same reasoning as gradlew, and it bites the same way: tools/check_store_metadata.sh runs on the
# Linux runner and a CRLF copy fails with `$'\r': command not found`, which names nothing useful.
# This repo is developed on Windows, so be explicit rather than relying on core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Golden screenshots and brand assets. Marking them binary keeps Git from trying to diff or
# convert them, and keeps a merge conflict in one from producing an unopenable file.
*.png binary

# Export packages are user content and have no business in the repo (see .gitignore), but if one
# is ever committed deliberately as a test fixture, it must not be mangled.
*.larova binary
